                <pb facs="0624" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2436: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-24T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            September 24, 1.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram of September 22, 5 p.m. The Ministry of Finance has given me
                    assurance verbally and in writing that Hsu En-yuan is authorized to renew the
                    existing Chicago Bank loan of $5,000,000 and also to negotiate for supplementary
                    loan of $25,000,000 contemplated by original contract.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
